Ticket #4471 contains **412 unique reports**, not one problem repeated 412 times. The export has 427 rows because 15 report IDs occur more than once; count each report ID once.

## Problems to split

| Problem | Reports | Evidence |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Shared parser flips dates for day-first tenants | **379** | The shared parser reads month first, while these tenants write day first. Reports arrive through the app, email, and booking forms. |
| Booking-v3 date hint conflicts with day-first tenants | **33** | Booking-v3 shows `MM/DD/YYYY`; day-first tenants expect `DD/MM/YYYY`. These are form reports from the booking-v3 tenants. |

Use the tenant's configured locale and booking form to classify a report. The browser locale and intake tag are guesses, not the source of truth. The five reports listed in `desk-notes.json` as one-day moves remain within the parser group under the export's tenant/channel rules; they are not an additional cause group.

The 379 parser reports and 33 booking-hint reports account for all 412 unique reports merged into #4471. File one ticket per problem so each fix and its affected report count can be tracked separately.

## Engineering update · October 5, 2026

The shared parser problem is fixed by `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The booking-v3 hint problem will not be fixed because the booking-v3 form has been retired.

Close the parser ticket as completed and the booking-v3 hint ticket as not planned.

